From 6fa3ca6f15ec0e2bcd168779dd29dd2be43a6960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:06:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: plumb ML1 measurements to analyzers
 (T-OR-058)

Physical-layer ML1 serving/neighbor cell measurements (PCI, EARFCN, RSRP)
are decoded by the diag layer but never reached analyzers: they are not
GSMTAP-convertible, so analyze_qmdl_message reported them as skipped packets.

Add an analyzer-facing `Ml1Measurement` (serving cell / neighbor cells,
decoupled from the on-wire deku structs, carrying no subscriber identity) with
`from_log_body`, a new `Analyzer::report_measurement` trait method, a Harness
fan-out, and an analyze_qmdl_message dispatch that surfaces the two ML1 log
bodies (0xb17f serving, 0xb180 neighbor) before the GSMTAP path.

report_measurement's default delegates to report_skipped_packet, so a
time-based analyzer that does not care about measurements keeps advancing its
clock automatically, and an analyzer that overrides it handles each ML1 packet
exactly once (no double dispatch). The measurement types are #[non_exhaustive]
with constructors, and report_measurement carries packet_num, so future
additions (RACH TA, RSRQ/RSSI) are not breaking changes.

This is additive and backward-compatible -- no public enum changes -- and is
the measurement input a cell-identity-consistency analyzer (T-OR-059) consumes.
Tests: from_log_body matches the diag ml1 vectors (pci/earfcn/rsrp), serving
and neighbor logs reach report_measurement, an overriding analyzer handles a
packet once, and ML1-only packets still make a time-based analyzer fire.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
